entation, then create\n15185|a new 2.0.0 transaction. A 2.0.0 peer or plugin rejects major 1 rather than\n15186|coercing its missing IDs or freezing an evolving status read.\n15187|\n15188|### 17.2 Reader/writer behavior\n15189|\n15190|A writer emits exactly the negotiated version. A reader:\n15191|\n15192|1. rejects an unsupported major;\n15193|2. accepts the same/lower supported minor;\n15194|3. preserves unknown namespaced extensions byte-for-byte when forwarding an\n15195|   immutable object;\n15196|4. rejects an unknown ownership/security enum that would affect behavior; and\n15197|5. MAY retain an unknown event as inert history but MUST NOT derive state from\n15198|   it.\n15199|\n15200|An <code>enabled = true</code> capability is valid only for the exact negotiated\n15201|contract and provider tuple or, for TerminalBackend capabilities, the exact\n15202|backend ID/implementation/protocol/generation/platform/OS evidence binding.\n15203|Version or binding mismatch changes it to conditional/unsupported and prevents\n15204|dependent activation.\n15205|\n15206|### 17.3 Immutable data migration\n15207|\n15208|Immutable objects MUST never be edited in place. A migration creates a new\n15209|schema-versioned object that references the prior object in\n15210|<code>extensions[\"works.relux.ax.migrated-from\"]</code>. That extension value is\n15211|a closed object containing exactly <code>schema_id:string</code>,\n15212|<code>schema_version:semver</code>, and <code>object_id:digest</code>. The writer\n15213|validates the new object and atomically advances a local reference. Old objects\n15214|remain available for rollback until retention policy allows collection.\n15215|\n15216|Configuration migration MUST create a backup, write a new file atomically, and\n15217|require <code>ax migrate config</code> for a major change. The CLI MUST NOT\n15218|silently rewrite a major-version config at startup.\n15219|\n15220|The derived SQLite index MAY be rebuilt at any time. It is ne