{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c969","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b119-7781-7bc0-8528-77290b455925"},"sequence":783,"recorded_at":1780531400001561,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b11c-7ebf-7100-a3aa-b371d198f461"},"task_id":"01a0b11c-7ebf-7100-a3aa-b371d198f461","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b11c-7ebf-7100-a3aa-b371d198f461","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-19-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n 1,60p internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main.go; echo \\\"===README-MEASURED===\\\"; grep -n \\\"Measured coverage\\\" -A 15 README.md | head -n 30; echo \\\"===LOGBOOK-HEAD===\\\"; head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check tracecheck flags, README coverage, LOGBOOK\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"// tracecheck is the headless CI entry point for AX specification-to-code\\n// ownership verification. It reports inventory coverage, not runtime support.\\npackage main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"flag\\\"\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"io\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n\\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/traceability\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tif err := run(os.Args[1:], os.Stdout); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, err)\\n\\t\\tos.Exit(1)\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\nfunc run(arguments []string, stdout io.Writer) error {\\n\\tflags := flag.NewFlagSet(\\\"tracecheck\\\", flag.ContinueOnError)\\n\\tflags.SetOutput(io.Discard)\\n\\troot := flags.String(\\\"root\\\", \\\".\\\", \\\"repository root\\\")\\n\\tvar sections sectionFlags\\n\\tflags.Var(&sections, \\\"section\\\", \\\"assigned normative section or same-section range; repeat for multiple scopes\\\")\\n\\tif err := flags.Parse(arguments); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif flags.NArg() != 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"unexpected positional arguments: %v\\\", flags.Args())\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvar report traceability.Report\\n\\tvar err error\\n\\tif len(sections) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treport, err = traceability.VerifyRepository(os.DirFS(*root))\\n\\t} else {\\n\\t\\treport, err = traceability.VerifyAssignedSections(os.DirFS(*root), sections)\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif _, err = fmt.Fprintf(\\n\\t\\tstdout,\\n\\t\\t\\\"traceability ok: contracts=%d normative_sections=%d acceptance_cases=%d fixtures=%d compatibility_contracts=%d assigned_scopes=%d\\\\n\\\",\\n\\t\\treport.Contracts,\\n\\t\\treport.NormativeSections,\\n\\t\\treport.AcceptanceCases,\\n\\t\\treport.Fixtures,\\n\\t\\treport.CompatibilityContracts,\\n\\t\\treport.AssignedScopes,\\n\\t); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\t// Coverage is printed as the measured ratio it was computed from. A gate\\n\\t// that reported \\\"sections owned\\\" would repeat the claim this line exists to\\n\\t// contradict.\\n\\t_, err = fmt.Fprintf(\\n===README-MEASURED===\\n3147:### Measured coverage of this repository\\n3148-\\n3149-`tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\\n3150-\\n3151-```text\\n3152-section coverage: bindings=65 full=2 partial=6 sliver=4 unevidenced=49 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=49/535\\n3153-```\\n3154-\\n3155-Sixty-five section bindings discharge 49 of the 535 normative clauses their\\n3156-sections carry. Two bindings are `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\\n3157-native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\\n3158-`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\\n3159-with the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\\n3160-refusal arm; and Section 2.4 at 4/4, bound to\\n3161-[`internal/sessprofile`](internal/sessprofile), whose derivation, checkpoint\\n3162-closure, fork projection, and mapping-failure clauses are discharged by the\\n===LOGBOOK-HEAD===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-219okr — dual-stack major negotiation (first leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/meshneg` (`Negotiate`/`LocalMajors`/`PeerOffer`/`Select` over `Refusal`/`Decision` pure data): generation-to-majors mapping (Config-1: 2; Config-2: 2,3; Config-3: 2,3,4; Config-4: exactly 5), single-major peer-offer validation against the framing major, highest-common selection, no-common-major refusal with registry-resolved `incompatible_protocol`/6 (unknown config: `invalid_config`/3), exact per-major contracts/namespaces/bound error versions rebuilt from rpcwire/axerror, and core-only peer exposure (`directory_mesh_unsupported`, `terminal_backend_unavailable`), never zero inventory. Frames nothing, admits nothing, pure/stateless. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- BINDING CHOICE: the RPC-4 exposure equivalent is the registered `terminal_backend_unavailable` (exit 6), not a minted token — Section 11.9 requires reporting evidence unsupported rather than empty and 17.4 requires reporting activation unavailable; the 1.3.0 exit-6 row carries exactly that code. Refusal/exposure exits resolve via `axerror.ExitCodeFor` under each code's introducing version; cross-version stability is asserted by test, not assumed.\\n- MUTANTS: 27 narrowing probes killed by named tests (neutral passed, harmless Detail-text control SURVIVED as designed; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`). Two initial SURVIVEDs were test gaps the harness caught: substituted-keys (same count, caught by membership loop, not length check) and peer-mixing-1-beside-common (unobservable without overlap) — both closed with new cases before the evidence run. Successor run RUN-260917-244f06 re-executed the harness: 27 killed, neutral passed, control SURVIVED (exit 0), and corrected the earlier \\\"28\\\" count.\\n- BOUNDS: v2 1-16 minor ranges select the major only (within-major minor selection future work); handshake sequencing stays with rpcwire decode + the responder; admission (identity/allowlist/generation) stays with TASK-260830-z1yxg9 with separation pinned by `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission`; no `ax` command, doctor result, or capability claimed. Traceability registry/digest untouched for the story final leaf (package-local TRACEABILITY.md only).\\n- AC: 11 of 11 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n- REV3 (RUN-260917-27bea1): rev1/rev2 CR validation both failed at suite command 5/27 on the sessquery race-timeout (default 10m, load-dependent, leaf-independent); trunk `888ae3d` fixed it systemically with an explicit `-timeout 25m`. Refreshed the candidate onto `888ae3d` (`refresh_advanced`, config restored to HEAD by hand, production untouched) and ran the full 27-command suite once: all exits 0, race gate 38 ok with sessquery 515.663s and no DATA RACE, meshneg 87.8%, mutants 27 killed / neutral passed / control SURVIVED.\\n- REV4 (RUN-260917-8fb798): rev3 review (RUN-260917-92b548) routed CHANGES REQUESTED with 3xP2 + 3xP3, all evidence/docs, production selection logic accepted unchanged. F1: exposure expectations now assert the literal `directory_mesh_unsupported` / `terminal_backend_unavailable` tokens at the Negotiate entry (no committed test derives from the production constants) + 2 same-exit swap plants. F2: new `TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration` drives unknown generations x every frame through Negotiate (invalid_config/3, zero Decision) + Negotiate-site fallback plant. F3: docs name `LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion` (not the normalized SchemaVersion) + `TestLocalMajorsTracksConfigVocabulary` pins the mapping against config.Version1/Version2/CurrentVersion/Version4 with a Decode-level normalization proof. F4: stated bound (non-rpc arrays validated by rpcwire decode, trusted here; direct callers must pass decode-produced hellos) pinned by `TestPeerOfferTrustsDecodedNonRPCArrays`; probe showed v2 lease 9.9.9 is admitted by decode too (valid range by design, not a hole). F5: frame rows 4.1.0/5.0.1/5.1.0 + 5.x-edge plant + unparseable-class bound stated. F6: TRACEABILITY 17.1 minor clause dropped. Harness now 31 narrowing killed / neutral passed / control SURVIVED (exit 0); 18/18 package tests green; full 27-command suite green (38 ok verbose/race/cover, race sessquery 370.955s no DATA RACE, meshneg 87.8%).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n- 2026-09-17 rev3 on `fc67abd`: pin `d3eca906…`, report 132 cases / 65 bindings / 7 unowned / 49 of 535 clauses; harness denominator 24 prior + 9 new; refresh-candidate completed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\\n\\n- SCOPE: executable proofs of the four story-pinned ownership invariants\\n  (union-order independence, loser preservation, clock non-authority,\\n  zero duplicate authorized owners) over `sessstate.Reduce`/`Compare`,\\n  `sessrepo.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`\\n  (Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10, v0.6.0). Final leaf of\\n  STORY-260830-1oqfec; carries the story-close traceability,\\n  README, and registry re-pin items.\\n- DEFECT (RED-first): `resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease\\n  against the transient arrival-order winner, so a loser's\\n  divergent-history evidence — even its presence — depended on union\\n  order (witness: `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain reports the loss in\\n  one arrival order and drops it in the other). FIX: two-pass\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 11305,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2827,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
