dmits 4 (producer `config4-admits-4`, R2/R3, my S3 variant), duplicate accepted (R1, S4, S5), key-count off by one (producer `shape-admits-extra-key`, R4; the −1 direction is S6, subsumed) — all killed except the documented equivalent.\\n7. **Docs and hygiene**: root README delta = 16 additive lines inside \\\"Mesh RPC envelopes and Host Channel\\\" (one paragraph + three tool rows), explicitly \\\"no `ax` command, doctor result, or capability claim\\\", measured-coverage subsection untouched (single hunk at :3522); LOGBOOK delta = 9 additive lines at the top of the first `## 2026-09-17` section, newest-first (duplicate `## 2026-09-17` headers lower in the file pre-exist on trunk); `internal/traceability`, `internal/axerror`, `task-board.config.json` untouched; changed paths exactly the 8 candidate paths; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the tree or the producer evidence tar (193 entries, real gzip); `gofmt -l` over all 579 Go files empty; `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=linux`/`GOOS=windows` builds exit 0; `git diff --check` clean for the candidate delta; `go test ./internal/meshneg -count=1 -v` 18/18 top-level, 184 `--- PASS` lines; `go test ./internal/meshneg ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel ./internal/axerror ./internal/config -count=1` ok; `-race` ok for meshneg/rpcwire/hostchannel; meshneg `-race -cover` 87.8%; `tracecheck` exit 0 (`clauses_discharged=49/535`, unchanged from the producer's cmd20 — the final leaf owns the registry); `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 with `catalog_gen.go` unchanged. AC ratio: 11 of 11 AC rows name a driving test at a production call site (matrix rev3); every named test exists in the verbose log. README/matrix/LOGBOOK/results agree on 31 narrowing probes, 18 tests, 87.8%.\\n8. **Full suite**: `go test ./... -count=1` rerun by me on the exact candidate tree: 38 ok, 0 FAIL, exit 0 (`logs/test-all.log`). Accepted from the runtime's bounded CR validation log (final line `required=27 green=27 failed=0 missing=0`) and the producer's per-command logs in the evidence tar (cmd0–cmd26, every `.exit` = 0; cmd3 38 ok / 0 FAIL; cmd4 race 38 ok, no DATA RACE; cmd5 38 ok; 14 fuzz smokes ok; cmd25 `task-board validate` exit 0 with 190 pre-existing MISSING_ACTIVITY warnings): the race run (`-timeout 25m`), the coverage run, the fuzz smokes, the JSON census and `task-board validate` were not rerun by me.\\n\\n## Checklist routing\\nAll producer items verified as checked; reviewer items \\\"Implementation matches AC\\\", \\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\", \\\"Tests green\\\", \\\"Gate … attacked, not read\\\" and \\\"verdict evidence added and status routed\\\" checked. Verdict recorded with `accept_cr(TASK-260830-219okr, revision=4, evidence=TASK-260830-219okr_review-verdict-rev4.md)` → `integrating`; checkpoint and integration belong to the bound producer role/archetype (`developer`/`implementer`) and the orchestrator.\\n\\n## Reviewer plants (committed-suite results, two runs)\\n\\n| Mutant | Kind | run1 | run2 | Expected committed killer | Failing committed tests (first 3) |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| R8-frame-admits-5.1 | narrowing | KILLED | KILLED | TestPeerOfferRefusals/frame-versions | TestPeerOfferRefusals/frame-versions, TestPeerOfferRefusals |\\n| R12-negotiate-unknown-config-falls-back-to-legacy | narrowing | KILLED | KILLED | TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration | TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration/unknown--x-2.0.0, TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration/unknown--x-3.0.0, TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration/unknown--x-4.0.0 |\\n| R19-directory-code-swap-same-exit | class-swap-same-exit | KILLED | KILLED | TestPeerExposure/2.0.0 | TestPeerExposure/2.0.0, TestPeerExposure |\\n| R20-backend-code-swap-same-exit | class-swap-same-exit | KILLED | KILLED | TestPeerExposure | TestPeerExposure/2.0.0, TestPeerExposure/3.0.0, TestPeerExposure |\\n| R1-dup-admitted | narrowing | KILLED | KILLED | TestPeerOfferRefusals/mixed/duplicate | TestPeerOfferRefusals/mixed/