rev3 surviving plant now dies twice in my own run; production selection logic is unchanged since rev3 (`negotiate.go` delta is doc comments only, reconstructed from the rev3/rev4 patches). My independent review found no P1 and no P2. Three P3 advisories are recorded below for the next producer on this Story (final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj or the wiring leaf); none is a production defect and none blocks acceptance.\\n\\n## (0) Rework verification — six findings graded\\n\\n| Finding | Grade | How I verified |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| F1 (P2) AC exposure tokens pinned circularly | **fixed** | `TestPeerExposure` (conformance_test.go:37-48) and `TestRefusalClassesResolveFromTheRegistry` (:152-153) now carry the literals `directory_mesh_unsupported` / `terminal_backend_unavailable`; no committed test references `meshneg.DirectoryUnsupportedCode`/`BackendEvidenceUnsupportedCode` (grep). Rev3 plants R19 (→`continuation_route_unavailable`) and R20 (→`terminal_backend_capability_unproven`) KILLED twice by `TestPeerExposure/2.0.0` (+`/3.0.0` for R20). Producer plants `exposure-directory-code-swap`/`exposure-backend-code-swap` present in `mutations.py` and KILLED in both of my harness runs. |\\n| F2 (P2) 6.6 unknown-generation refusal pinned only at the helper | **fixed** | `TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration` (negotiate_test.go:278-305) drives `Negotiate` with 8 unknown generations × 4 pinned frames (32 subtests) asserting `invalid_config`/3, `ReasonUnknownConfig`, `ErrUnknownConfig`, a zero `Decision{}` (`reflect.DeepEqual`) and empty offer facts. Rev3 plant R12 (Negotiate-site fallback to `[2 3 4]`) KILLED twice (33 failing subtests). Producer plant `negotiate-unknown-falls-back` present and KILLED. |\\n| F3 (P2) generation input named the normalized field | **fixed** | negotiate.go:170-177 and :463-468 name `config.LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion` and warn against `Configuration.SchemaVersion`; `TestLocalMajorsTracksConfigVocabulary` (negotiate_test.go:170-224) pins `LocalMajors` against `config.Version1/Version2/CurrentVersion/Version4`, decodes minimal v1/v2/v3 documents through `config.Decode` proving `SourceVersion` carries the generation while `Value.SchemaVersion` normalizes to `CurrentVersion`, and proves the trap (SchemaVersion input yields a different major set for v1/v2). Field and vocabulary re-verified in the landed owner (`internal/config/schema.go:15-22,57-60`). |\\n| F4 (P3) `PeerOffer` re-validation over-claim | **fixed (stated-bound option)** | Doc comment (negotiate.go:253-257), package README (PeerOffer row), TRACEABILITY (\\\"Non-rpc hello array values\\\" bound) and the `directHello` comment all state that non-`rpc` array values are validated by rpcwire decode and trusted; `TestPeerOfferTrustsDecodedNonRPCArrays` pins both halves (tampered v3/v4/v5 `session_event` admitted by `PeerOffer`, refused by `rpcwire.EncodeRequest` with `ErrHello`; v2 `lease=[\\\"9.9.9\\\"]` admitted by both — I confirm the v2 half is valid 1–16 range input by design, not a hole). |\\n| F5 (P3) frame gate measured only at 2.x/3.x edges; unparseable class | **fixed** | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/frame-versions` now carries `4.1.0`, `5.0.1`, `5.1.0` (and `garbage`); rev3 plant R8 (`\\\"5.1.0\\\": 5`) KILLED twice; producer plant `frame-admits-5.1` present and KILLED; my own `S1-frame-admits-3.0.1` and `S2-frame-admits-4.1.0` KILLED twice. The unparseable-version class (`incompatible_protocol`/6 here vs 15.1 `transport_failure`, unreachable through `rpcwire` decode whose `major()` accepts only the four pinned strings — re-read at `internal/rpcwire/envelope.go:56-69`) is stated in the doc comment, README and TRACEABILITY. |\\n| F6 (P3) TRACEABILITY 17.1 wording | **fixed** | 17.1 row now reads \\\"No major selected by coercion\\\" (PeerOffer mixing refusal, Select); within-major minor selection remains only in the stated-bounds table. |\\n\\n## Findings (advisory, P3 — none blocks acceptance)\\n\\n### N1 — P3 — `PeerOffer` key-membership gate pinned at one hand-picked key\\n- Shape: hand-picked member of a source-defined set (`references/negative-evidence.md`, \\\"Derive Completeness From An Independent Source\\\"; repo memory \\\"duplicate-member gate pinned per key\\\").\\n- Gate: negotiate.go:279-283 (`for key := range profile { if _, ok := hello.Contracts[key]; !ok { … } }`). The committed negative test `TestPeerOfferRefusals/shape/substituted-key` substitutes only `lease`, and the producer plant `shape-admits-missing-lease` is aimed at that same witnessed member. Per-key sweep (`key_sweep_rev4.py`, 25 plants `key != \\\"<K>\\\"`, committed suite): **1 of 25 keys killed (`lease`)**; `rpc` is subsumed by the rpc-length arm (`len(offered) < 1`), so the ratio for the membership gate proper is 1 of 24 non-rpc keys. My spec-derived probe `TestReviewSpecDerivedShapesRev4` (substitutes every key of every frame, 88 combinations) kills S7/S8/S9.\\n- Impact bound: production behavior is correct (the loop is uniform), and the composed production path is closed by `rpcwire` decode's own key check (`internal/rpcwire/hello.go:94-106`); no production caller of `meshneg` exists yet. Fix (next producer): derive the substituted-key and missing-key cases from `rpcwire.ContractProfile(frame)` for every frame and every key, so any per-key exemption reddens.\\n\\n### N2 — P3 — `Refusal.Local` on offer-originated refusals is unpinned through `Negotiate`\\n- negotiate.go:490-493 copies the local offer into a `PeerOffer` refusal; the doc (`Refusal.Local`, :116-118) makes it a reported fact. Plant S12 (`refusal.Local = nil`) SURVIVED the committed suite twice (`TestRefusalShape` asserts `Local` only on a `Select` no-common-major refusal; `TestNoFallbackSurface/extension-member` asserts `Reason` only). My `TestReviewHostileOffersRev4` asserts `Local == LocalMajors(generation)` on all 31 malformed-offer rows and kills it.\\n- Fix: assert `refusal.Local` in one shape and one mixed case driven through `Negotiate`.\\n\\n### N3 — P3 — `Select` local-side vocabulary member `1` unpinned (direct-call surface only)\\n- negotiate.go:329-338 refuses local majors outside 2/3/4/5; plant S14 (`major < 1`) SURVIVED twice: the refused table has `local-names-6`, `negative-major` (-2) and `zero-major` (0) on the local side but no `1`. Unreachable through `Negotiate` (`LocalMajors` never yields 1); only a direct `Select` caller sees it. My `TestReviewSelectVocabularyBothSidesRev4` (-1/0/1/6/7/99 beside a common major, both sides) kills it.\\n- Fix: one `refuse-local-names-1` row.\\n\\n## Verified (reviewer instruments; every log in the evidence archive)\\n\\n1. **Spec fidelity** (`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md` sha256 `74504539…896b` == `specpin.DocumentSHA256V060`; v0.7.0 has not landed — `internal/specdoc` holds v0.6.0 only, so the v0.6.0 citations stand). Extracted myself and diffed against negotiate.go: generation→majors (6.4/6.5/6.6/11.8/11.9: Config-1 [2], Config-2 [2 3], Config-3 [2 3 4], Config-4 exactly [5]; \\\"Unknown/missing/partial configuration … is a refusal, never legacy selection\\\" → `invalid_config`/3; \\\"Legacy RPC 2/3/4 dual-stack obligations apply only to explicitly legacy installations; they never require a Config-4 endpoint to accept legacy\\\"); per-major hello maps derived from the spec's own JSON blocks by `TestReviewSpecDerivedShapesRev4` (11.2 request/response 14 keys, 11.8 24 keys, 11.9 25 keys, 11.10.1 = the 11.9 map with `rpc [\\\"5.0.0\\\"]`) — the `Decision.Contracts` produced by `Negotiate` is `reflect.DeepEqual` to each spec block, 4 of 4 majors; namespaces 6/7/8/8 (11.8/11.9 prose); Structured Error bindings 1.0.0/1.2.0/1.3.0/1.3.0 (11.2, 11.8, 11.9, 11.10.1) via `axerror.BindingFor`; \\\"Every v2 [1..6] bound … MUST NOT be used inside a v3 frame\\\" → the 14-key map inside a v3/v4/v5 frame refuses `contract_shape`; 11.8 \\\"exposes the peer as directory_mesh_unsupported, never as zero inventory\\\" and the 11.9 analogue (\\\"reports TerminalBackend evidence unsupported rather than empty\\\"; v4/v2 \\\"reports both … unsupported\\\"); 6.6 no-fallback sentence. **Binding choice** `terminal_backend_unavailable`: 11.9 names no literal code (my probe logs this from the text), 17.4 requires \\\"report activation unavailable rather than omit the Session\\\", and the 15.3 Structured Error 1.3.0 exit-6 row registers exactly `terminal_backend_unavailable` — a registered class, not an invention; `internal/axerror` is untouched by the CR (changed paths are exactly the 8 candidate paths), so no code was minted. Refusing a multi-major `rpc` array is not a literal clause; it follows 17.1 (\\\"MUST NOT select a major by coercion\\\") and the task brief's \\\"refuse … any cross-major mixing\\\", and `TestSemverAgreementWithRPCWire/other-major-*` records the deliberate divergence from decode.\\n2. **Pair table**: 64 rows through `Negotiate` (`TestReviewPairTableRev4`: 16 known-generation pairs — selected major == the peer's framing major when it is in the generation's set, with the exact spec map, exposure flags/literal tokens/exit 6, bound error version — else `incompatible_protocol`/6/`no_common_major` with `Local`/`Peer` facts and a zero `Decision`; 48 unknown-generation pairs, 12 generations × 4 frames → `invalid_config`/3, zero `Decision`, no offer facts). Exits re-derived through `axerror.ExitCodeFor(1.0.0, …)`. 37 hostile-offer subtests (`TestReviewHostileOffersRev4`): v3/v4/v5 frames carrying the 14-key v2 map, a v2 frame carrying 24/25 keys, v5 carrying the v3 map, v5↔v4 map swaps (refused at the rpc-major check, `mixed_major`), unsorted (`2.1.0,2.0.0` and the lexical `2.9.0,2.10.0` — negotiator and `rpcwire` decode both compare lexically, `hello.go:104`, so they agree), duplicate (2- and 3-element), multi-major 2+3 / 2..5 / 4+5-in-v5, `6.0.0` in v5, `5.1.0` in v5, `1.0.0`/`v2.0.0`/range syntax, empty/nil/missing/substituted `rpc`, extension/fallback/error/host_channel keys, nil/empty contracts, 17 entries; frame `6.0.0` for every generation; 20 frame-version edges (`2.0.1` … `5.1.0`, prerelease/build/v-prefix/leading-zero/whitespace); `5.0.0`→Config-3; legacy 2/3/4→Config-4; env (`AX_RPC_MAJOR=2`, `AX_ALLOW_LEGACY=1`, `AX_HOST_CHANNEL=0`, `AX_CONFIG_GENERATION=3.0.0`) + argv (`--legacy --rpc-major=2 --allow-legacy --host-channel 0`) cannot talk a Config-4 endpoint below 5; five failed legacy attempts then a valid RPC 5 offer (accepted, then legacy still refused) and three RPC-5 refusals on a Config-3 node then a valid RPC 4 offer (accepted). Every refusal: exact class/exit, zero `Decision`, `Peer`=0 and `Local`==the generation's set. `Negotiate` frames nothing: negotiate.go contains no `Encode`/`Decode`/`os.`/`net.`/`time.` reference (grep count 0).\\n3. **Core-only exposure**: Config-1/2/3 × v2 → `directory_mesh_unsupported`/6 + `terminal_backend_unavailable`/6; Config-2/3 × v3 → directory negotiated (no code), backend `terminal_backend_unavailable`/6; Config-3 × v4 and Config-4 × v5 → both negotiated, no codes (`TestReviewExposureLiteralTokensRev4`, 7 pairs, literal strings). Structural pin reddens: R16 (`FeatureActivation` gains `Inventory int`) and R17 (`PeerView` gains `Count int`) KILLED twice by `TestExposureCarriesNoInventory`; the JSON view of `Decision.Peer` carries no numeric member other than `ExitCode` and no collection. `TestReviewDecisionNeverCopiesPeerBytesRev4`: a decode-valid v2 range offer (`rpc [2.0.0, 2.1.0, 2.2.0-rc.1]`, `lease [1.0.0, 1.1.0]`) selects 2 with the pinned profile, and writing into the returned map changes neither a later decision nor the `rpcwire` profile.\\n4. **Separation from admission**: no production importer of `internal/meshneg` (grep; only its own tests); `internal/hostchannel` does not import it, and every exported hostchannel entry (`hostchannel-exported-signatures.log`, 31 signatures) takes typed `hosttrust`/`config`/`tls`/`Stream`/`peeridentity` inputs — no `any`/interface parameter exists through which a `Decision` could be presented as an admission token. Config-4 cannot be talked below RPC 5 by any frame, map, env, argv or retry sequence (item 2). `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission` (13 identity-adjacent variants incl. decode-invalid values) holds.\\n5. **Purity**: `go list -f '{{.Imports}}'` is exactly `errors fmt regexp slices strconv strings` + `axerror rpcwire`; the four owner functions consulted (`ContractProfile`, `Namespaces`, `ExitCodeFor`, `BindingFor`) are pure table/map lookups (read); the transitive closure reaches `os/io/net/time/rand/exec` only through the owners, which the README correctly scopes to direct imports. `TestNegotiationIsDeterministic` holds. Stated crash/idempotency bound accepted.\\n6. **Mutation**: producer harness re-executed twice in the isolated copy — 33 rows = 31 narrowing KILLED (each by its named `expected_test`), neutral passed, `detail-text` control SURVIVED, exit 0, no `__pycache__`; identical to the producer's `results.json`. Reviewer harness (`review_mutants_rev4.py`, 36 rows, two full runs, identical): the 4 rev3 survivors KILLED ×2; the 12 other rev3 plants KILLED ×2; 18 new plants — 11 KILLED ×2 (S1 frame 3.0.1, S2 frame 4.1.0, S3 Config-4 admits 3, S4 duplicate admitted for the 2.0.0 pair only, S5 sort check skips the first pair, S10 v4 exact exempt, S11 highest-common skips 4, S13 refusal drops the peer fact, S15 directory activation inverted, S16 Config-2 admits 4 instead of 3, S17 empty-string generation admitted), 5 SURVIVED ×2 (S7/S8/S9 → N1, S12 → N2, S14 → N3; each KILLED by my probe suite in `survivor_control_rev4.py`), 2 equivalent SURVIVED (S6 one-fewer-key subsumed by the membership loop; S18 hardcoded exit 6 equals the registry value) also surviving my probes; controls C1/C2 SURVIVED everywhere. Of the brief's four suggested arms: highest→lowest (producer `select-picks-lowest` + my S11), Config-4 admits 4 (producer `config4-admits-4`, R2/R3, my S3 variant), duplicate accepted (R1, S4, S5), key-count off by one (producer `shape-admits-extra-key`, R4; the −1