{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d955","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b119-7781-7bc0-8528-77290b455925"},"sequence":2821,"recorded_at":1780531400005637,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b135-460f-7ed1-8617-e51ba629db86"},"task_id":"01a0b135-460f-7ed1-8617-e51ba629db86","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b135-460f-7ed1-8617-e51ba629db86","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-4qojoz/worktree/README.md`.\n(3488 line(s) above)\n3489|## Mesh RPC envelopes and Host Channel\n3490|\n3491|[`internal/rpcwire`](internal/rpcwire) validates structural Mesh RPC\n3492|2/3/4/5 request/response envelopes: request-ID and version correlation,\n3493|14-key hello maps with nonce echo and line/object limit floors, the exact\n3494|historical 24/25-key maps and 6/7/8-namespace inventory vocabulary, static\n3495|historical Structured Error bindings (1.0.0/1.2.0/1.3.0, with 1.3.0 for\n3496|RPC majors 4 and 5), and the 8 MiB line bound. RPC 5.0.0 reuses the\n3497|exact RPC-4 shapes with `contracts.rpc` `[\"5.0.0\"]`.\n3498|[`internal/hostchannel`](internal/hostchannel) is the authenticated\n3499|consumer: mutual TLS 1.3 with ALPN `ax-host/1` over an abstract ordered\n3500|binary stream, enrolled-certificate identity from hosttrust snapshots,\n3501|authorized hello on both roles under the current generation, dispatch\n3502|and mutation boundaries, and one framed Error 1.3.0 refusal per\n3503|pre-hello violation. The ten HC-* gates of Section 11.10.4 run as\n3504|executable positive/negative fixture families. There is no `ax`\n3505|command, SSH process launch, or provider plugin; launch selection is a\n3506|computed Configuration-4 argv only.\n3507|\n3508|The hostile-network conformance suite (`internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go`,\n3509|`internal/hostchannel/hostile_carrier_test.go`, acceptance case `AC-HOST-001`)\n3510|re-derives the seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call`\n3511|entries — unknown peers, key changes, spoofed host IDs, disconnects at every\n3512|phase boundary, replay, oversized frames, disclosure mismatches — and measures\n3513|the product-gate rows: a real OpenSSH loopback carrier lane (unprivileged\n3514|`sshd` on 127.0.0.1, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS\n3515|records first, no PTY, bounded stderr), timeout/race, custody, revocation and\n3516|generation fencing, migration/downgrade refusals, both role failures,\n3517|stale/failed reads, and recovery bypasses. Every vector pins the Section 15\n3518|refusal class and carries a before/after state census. Stated bounds, recorded\n3519|as not executed rather than passed: native Tailscale SSH, platform lanes other\n3520|than the test host, and the Section 11.10.3 one-second self-close of an idle\n3521|stream with zero traffic (measured: the product fences the next dispatch and\n3522|`WatchGeneration` reports the commit; `serveLoop` carries no background\n3523|watchdog). Section 11.10.5 upstream vectors are source evidence only.\n3524|\n3525|[`internal/meshneg`](internal/meshneg) selects the single Mesh RPC major for\n3526|one peer connection from the local configuration generation and the peer's\n3527|decoded hello: Config-4 offers exactly RPC 5, legacy generations offer the\n3528|historical dual-stack sets, the peer offer must agree with its framing major,\n3529|and a disjoint pair refuses no-common-major with `incompatible_protocol`\n3530|(exit 6) from actually known inputs. A selection carries the exact pinned\n3531|contracts map, namespace vocabulary, and bound Structured Error version for\n3532|its major, and reports above-core activation the selection does not carry as\n3533|explicitly unsupported (`directory_mesh_unsupported`,\n3534|`terminal_backend_unavailable`), never as zero inventory. Outcomes are pure\n3535|data: nothing is framed, connected, advertised, or admitted here. There is\n3536|no `ax` command, doctor result, or capability claim.\n3537|\n3538|| Tool / check | Exact command | Output |\n3539|| --- | --- | --- |\n3540|| RPC/host-channel behavior | `go test ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel -count=1 -v` | stdout; `.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/` logs |\n3541|| Major-negotiation behavior | `go test ./internal/meshneg -count=1 -v` | stdout; `.temp/TASK-260830-219okr/` logs |\n3542|| Major-negotiation races and coverage | `go test ./internal/meshneg -race -count=1 -cover` | Race diagnostics and measured package coverage |\n3543|| Major-negotiation narrowing | `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/meshneg/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-219okr/mutations-meshneg` | 31 narrowing probes killed by named tests plus neutral and harmless SURVIVED controls, in per-plant raw logs and mutant tables; source originals remain untouched |\n3544|| RPC/host-channel races and coverage | `go test ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel -race -count=1 -cover` | Race diagnostics and measured package coverage |\n3545|| RPC/host-channel narrowing | `python3 internal/rpcwire/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/mutations-rpcwire` and `python3 internal/hostchannel/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/mutations-hostchannel` | Applied compiling overlays, JSON events, real exits, named failing tests and mutant tables; source originals remain untouched |\n3546|| Hostile-network conformance | `go test ./internal/hostchannel -run 'TestHostile' -count=1 -v` | Per-vector refusal classes, census assertions, and the OpenSSH loopback lane (skips with an asserted reason when `sshd` cannot bind); `.temp/TASK-260830-2x16gz/` logs |\n3547|| Hostile narrowing | `python3 internal/hostchannel/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-2x16gz/mutations-hostchannel` | Nine added narrowing probes killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors, plus the shipped suite, in per-plant raw logs and mutant tables; source originals remain untouched |\n3548|| RPC fuzz smoke | `go test ./internal/rpcwire -run '^$' -fuzz '^FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes$' -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1` | stdout and task log |","final_result":true}}}
