{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d97f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b119-7781-7bc0-8528-77290b455925"},"sequence":2842,"recorded_at":1780531400005679,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b135-67ec-74b2-aefe-25c818b3e75c"},"task_id":"01a0b135-67ec-74b2-aefe-25c818b3e75c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b135-67ec-74b2-aefe-25c818b3e75c","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-4qojoz/worktree/README.md`.\n(3146 line(s) above)\n3147|### Measured coverage of this repository\n3148|\n3149|`tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\n3150|\n3151|```text\n3152|section coverage: bindings=65 full=2 partial=6 sliver=4 unevidenced=49 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=49/535\n3153|```\n3154|\n3155|Sixty-five section bindings discharge 49 of the 535 normative clauses their\n3156|sections carry. Two bindings are `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\n3157|native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\n3158|`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\n3159|with the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\n3160|refusal arm; and Section 2.4 at 4/4, bound to\n3161|[`internal/sessprofile`](internal/sessprofile), whose derivation, checkpoint\n3162|closure, fork projection, and mapping-failure clauses are discharged by the\n3163|profile derivation, heads, fork-pair, and mapping-resolution acceptance\n3164|cases), six are\n3165|`partial` (Section 13.13 at 9/11, bound to\n3166|[`internal/matjournal`](internal/matjournal) with the\n3167|[`internal/crashgate`](internal/crashgate) conformance harness, whose\n3168|undischarged clauses `13.13#4` and `13.13#5` are the rollback/parked\n3169|visibility sentences through event, CLI/status, audit, and\n3170|lifecycle-projection surfaces this repository has no binary or projection to\n3171|produce; Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\n3172|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\n3173|is the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; Section\n3174|5.3 at 7/8, bound to\n3175|[`internal/sessrepo`](internal/sessrepo), whose undischarged clause `5.3#5`\n3176|is the initiator-union maximum no takeover flow computes yet; Section\n3177|15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\n3178|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\n3179|the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\n3180|binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\n3181|TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no\n3182|provider plugin, and advertises no Structured Error as a TerminalBackend\n3183|capability. Structural RPC hello frames are built by\n3184|[`internal/rpcwire`](internal/rpcwire), which rejects an error map key, and\n3185|consumed by the authenticated [`internal/hostchannel`](internal/hostchannel)\n3186|handshake, which frames failures only as Error envelopes and never as hello\n3187|keys; neither clause is enumerated against an acceptance case, so both stay\n3188|undischarged. The closed 16-capability admission registry in\n3189|[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) gates which operations\n3190|an admitted probe may confer; it is never advertised on an RPC hello path and\n3191|carries no Structured Error code, so the prohibition holds and the clause\n3192|stays undischarged. The same package carries the Section 4 lifecycle,\n3193|attach, entrypoint, replication, and historical-translation conformance\n3194|harness (`conformance.go`, exercised by `conformance_test.go`) and an\n3195|AST-derived refusal-arm inventory (`refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`) that\n3196|requires every production refusal arm to be declared with a resolving named\n3197|asserting test in both directions; behavioral proof stays with each row's\n3198|named test, which the inventory resolves textually; and Section 7.7 at 3/4,\n3199|bound to [`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost), whose undischarged clause\n3200|`7.7#2` is the machine-local-alias sentence - the omit rule is enforced, but a\n3201|shell word that expands to unrestricted mode without spelling a table token is\n3202|beyond argv inspection),\n3203|four are\n3204|`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\n3205|enforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\n3206|implementation; Section 5.5 at 1/3, whose discharged negative-battery clause\n3207|is enforced by identity creation and checking while the opaque-map content\n3208|rule stays half-decided; Section 8 at 4/12, whose discharged probe,\n3209|label-integrity, and row-separation clauses are enforced by the resume tuple\n3210|gate and the native-resume smoke while every materialization rule stays\n3211|unimplemented; and Section 2.2 at 4/22, bound to\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
