{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d9b1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b119-7781-7bc0-8528-77290b455925"},"sequence":2867,"recorded_at":1780531400005729,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b135-8571-76f1-90a9-68f312b61e30"},"task_id":"01a0b135-8571-76f1-90a9-68f312b61e30","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b135-8571-76f1-90a9-68f312b61e30","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-4qojoz/worktree/README.md`.\n(3210 line(s) above)\n3211|unimplemented; and Section 2.2 at 4/22, bound to\n3212|[`internal/fencing`](internal/fencing), whose discharged clauses are the\n3213|single-owner, replica-restraint, winning-epoch-carriage, and\n3214|losing-event-rejection invariants while the replication, secret, store,\n3215|and directory invariants have no implementation), four are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.12, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n3216|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n3217|and forty-nine are `unevidenced`. Seven sections are recorded unowned.\n3218|All 13 sections added by v0.6.0 name pending task owners in the reviewed\n3219|registry gaps; these assignments grant no runtime admission. The\n3220|[adoption ownership map](internal/traceability/adoption-v0.6.0.md) separates\n3221|shared runtime APIs, their callers, product conformance and upstream source\n3222|publication validators, and preserves historical acceptance obligations.\n3223|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\n3224|`-section 2.4` and nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its\n3225|ratio and its gap.\n3226|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n3227|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n3228|\n3229|Two admitted bindings out of sixty-five cover five clauses, and that is\n3230|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n3231|ever be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\n3232|native-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\n3233|`TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` the legacy refusal arm,\n3234|both registered against the `config-versioned-readers` acceptance case.\n3235|Section 2.4 is the first multi-clause admission: its four clauses are\n3236|discharged by the `sessprofile-derive`, `sessprofile-derive-heads`,\n3237|`sessprofile-fork-pair`, and `provhost-mapping-resolution` acceptance cases.\n3238|\n3239|That is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\n3240|`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\n3241|`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\n3242|binding with its exact measured ratio, so a section that becomes covered has to\n3243|leave those tables deliberately. Five further gaps the disclosure surfaced:\n3244|Section 15.2's code-to-exit registry is implemented in\n3245|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) and checked row by row, and\n3246|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult) now maps a failure to that exact\n3247|process status through `Emit` and `ExitStatus`, but nothing in the tree calls\n3248|`os.Exit` with it - the only `os.Exit` calls are the `exit(1)` failure paths of\n3249|`cataloggen` and `tracecheck` - so clause `14.2#6` stays undischarged until an\n3250|`ax` binary exists; Section 7.3's closed Provider Manifest exists only as a catalog\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
