{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000db0f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b119-7781-7bc0-8528-77290b455925"},"sequence":3042,"recorded_at":1780531400006079,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b136-35af-7402-beea-a3206a1fb4a9"},"task_id":"01a0b136-35af-7402-beea-a3206a1fb4a9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b136-35af-7402-beea-a3206a1fb4a9","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-4qojoz/worktree/README.md`.\n(3043 line(s) above)\n3044|## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n3045|\n3046|[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\n3047|repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\n3048|[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\n3049|registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\n3050|contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 132\n3051|executable acceptance cases, 65 exact section bindings with their declared\n3052|coverage, 7 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\n3053|Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\n3054|and the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\n3055|The generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\n3056|contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\n3057|binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\n3058|malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\n3059|\n3060|The production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\n3061|metadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\n3062|owner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\n3063|self-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\n3064|GitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\n3065|build:\n3066|\n3067|```bash\n3068|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n3069|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\n3070|```\n3071|\n3072|The repeated `-section` form is the Story-scope production gate. It resolves\n3073|each assigned subsection, and every heading in a same-top-level range, against\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
