{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dd57","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b119-7781-7bc0-8528-77290b455925"},"sequence":3334,"recorded_at":1780531400006663,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"13d59c78-6f33-4ca9-9b77-41caa4df923d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b138-5f89-7673-920a-6add58d35b5e"},"task_id":"01a0b138-5f89-7673-920a-6add58d35b5e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b138-5f89-7673-920a-6add58d35b5e","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-17\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-18\n+\n+### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj: adversarial closure\n+- DELIVERED (test-only; no production behavior file changed): `internal/rpcwire/adversarial_test.go` (closed-body member/bound sweeps for the two parsed bodies, per-member namespace vocabulary + 30-cell mismatch matrix, unknown-field sweep over every closed shape, both §17.1 extension directions, correlation classes, major-1 rejection, error-schema-not-negotiated, framing bounds) and `internal/rpcwire/fuzz_adversarial_test.go` (FuzzClosedOperationBodies over the 24-op vocabulary, FuzzNamespaceVocabulary with a spec-transcribed oracle, FuzzUnknownFields over raw lines — each with a planted control that FAILS, then removed); `internal/meshneg/adversarial_test.go` (N1 per-key sweep for every frame/key through Negotiate, N2 Local-fact pins, six no-coercion shapes + major-1 through the composed entry) plus the N3 `refuse-local-names-1` row. Registered the 3 fuzz targets as bounded validation commands (task-board.config.json +3 rows, stated explicitly).\n+- N1-N3 (inherited P3s, all closed): membership sweep kills per-key exemption plants at every key (reviewer's S7/S8/S9 class); Local==LocalMajors(generation) asserted on all shape+mixed rows (kills S12); local-1 row placed beside a common major after the first revision proved unobservable (disjoint refusal subsumes the plant — the harness caught it, fixed before the evidence run). Reachability bound stated: LocalMajors never yields 1.\n+- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 39 killed / neutral passed / new error-text SURVIVED control (exit 0). One honest sentinel-swap row (correlation-id-maps-frame) labeled as swap, not narrowing. Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\n+- TRACEABILITY: upgraded 4 unevidenced bindings (11.2 partial 3/5, 11.3 sliver 1/27, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4) with 6 new acceptance cases incl. story case `story-4qojoz-mesh-negotiation` over the real conformance suite; prior owners' cases merged, none orphaned; 17.2/17.3 keep existing unevidenced owners. Digest re-derived `1500e259…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `57/535` (+8); section-scoped runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate table updates in traceability_test.go/main_test.go + README figures/paragraph (138 cases).\n+- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque (no initiator/lease revalidation entry exists); no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id is correlation-only (no responder replay cache — replay/idempotency evidence adopted from matjournal `TestCreateReplayAndConflict`/crash suite); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 26 of 26 rows driven or explicitly bounded (matrix in the outcome evidence).\n+- PROCESS: a fuzzer \"finding\" on first smoke was an oracle bug (JSON replaces invalid UTF-8; guarded with utf8.ValidString). Fuzz controls must use `-fuzztime=100x`: `10x` caps TOTAL execs including seeds, so late seeds never run (control falsely passed until rerun). A stray shell `>` typo truncated `internal/matjournal/journal_test.go` mid-session; restored byte-identical from the checkpoint (`git checkout --`, verified via clean status); no evidence depends on the incident window.\n+- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+\n+## 2026-09-17\n","final_result":true}}}
